{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Pattern Feature Mining.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Pattern Feature Mining.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sequential pattern feature mining sequential pattern feature mining","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Pattern Feature Mining.md","fileName":"Sequential Pattern Feature Mining.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sequential Pattern Feature Mining","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 21:00\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Sequence and Network Classification]] · [[Sequence Feature Engineering]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Sequence and Network Classification","Sequence Feature Engineering","dataclassification.pdf","featureengineeringformachinelearninganddataanalytics.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Pattern Feature Mining.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Pattern Feature Mining.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sequential pattern feature mining sequential pattern feature mining","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Pattern Feature Mining.md","fileName":"Sequential Pattern Feature Mining.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sequential Pattern Feature Mining","heading":"Sequential Pattern Feature Mining","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Sequential pattern feature mining discovers ordered symbol patterns and converts their occurrence into classifier inputs. Class-sensitive criteria favor subsequences that distinguish labels rather than merely appearing frequently overall.\n\nThe candidate space grows combinatorially as patterns lengthen. Minimum support, upper bounds, closed-pattern constraints, and wrapper evaluation reduce the search while preserving features likely to improve classification.\n\nA complete pattern-defined feature also specifies how matches become values, such as binary presence, cumulative frequency, positional indicators, or windowed counts. Mining and mapping are therefore distinct design decisions.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Sequence and Network Classification","Sequence Feature Engineering","dataclassification.pdf","featureengineeringformachinelearninganddataanalytics.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Pattern Feature Mining.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Pattern Feature Mining.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"sequential pattern feature mining sequential pattern feature mining","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Sequential Pattern Feature Mining.md","fileName":"Sequential Pattern Feature Mining.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Sequential Pattern Feature Mining","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[dataclassification.pdf]]\n\n[[featureengineeringformachinelearninganddataanalytics.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Sequence and Network Classification","Sequence Feature Engineering","dataclassification.pdf","featureengineeringformachinelearninganddataanalytics.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}